From: zswll2 <zswll2@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 12:02:05 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 06/32] feat(desktop): edge-swipe gesture opens/closes the
 narrow-viewport drawer
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

No touch gesture existed anywhere in the app — on a phone the collapsed
session sidebar was reachable only through the 44px titlebar button.

- classifyEdgeSwipe(): pure threshold contract (start x<=24, |dy|<=40,
  |dx|>=60; close is direction-gated on the open drawer) with boundary
  unit tests at every threshold edge
- useEdgeSwipeDrawer(): document-level pure-observer listeners — all
  passive, never preventDefault, so the transcript's own scroll is never
  fought; gated on SIDEBAR_COLLAPSE_MEDIA_QUERY so desktop sees zero
  behavior; a second finger (pinch) invalidates the gesture
- gesture input is the drawer's VISIBILITY (the overlay's rendered node),
  not the pane's open flag — the flag defaults true while the narrow
  drawer is hidden, which would neuter every open swipe (found in E2E)
- state changes flow only through store/layout's setSidebarOpen
